## Overview

Valentine's Garage is an Android app that digitises the vehicle intake and repair workflow at a garage. Mechanics can check trucks in, record their condition and kilometres, and collaboratively tick off repair tasks — preventing work from going undone because one mechanic assumed another had handled it. The admin (Valentine) can view a live report of fleet status and mechanic activity.

---

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| **Vehicle Check-In** | Record plate number, odometer reading, condition, and select repairs needed |
| **Repair Tasks** | Each selected repair at check-in becomes an individual task for mechanics to tick off |
| **Collaborative Tasks** | Any mechanic can open any in-service truck and mark tasks done with notes |
| **Fleet Dashboard** | Live counts of trucks in repair, completed, and needing urgent attention |
| **Trucks In Service Screen** | Dedicated screen listing all active trucks with progress bars — tap to open tasks |
| **Admin Reports** | Full fleet statistics, per-truck repair progress, and per-mechanic activity breakdown |
| **Role-Based Routing** | Admins go to Reports; mechanics go to Dashboard on login |
| **Duplicate Plate Guard** | If a plate is already in service, prompts mechanic to open existing tasks or create a new entry |
| **Auto-Refresh** | Dashboard and Reports refresh automatically every time the screen is revisited |

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | Kotlin |
| UI Framework | Jetpack Compose (Material 3) |
| Database | Supabase (PostgreSQL) |
| DB Client | `io.github.jan-tennert.supabase:postgrest-kt` v2.6.0 |
| Serialisation | `kotlinx.serialization` |
| Async | Kotlin Coroutines |
| Min SDK | Android 8.0 (API 26) |
| Target SDK | Android 15 (API 35) |

