## Database Schema

The app uses three tables hosted on **Supabase**:

### `Users`
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | uuid | Primary key |
| name | text | Full name |
| email | text | Login username |
| role | text | `mechanic` or `admin` |
| pin | text | Numeric PIN password |
| created_at | timestamp | Auto-set by Supabase |

### `trucks`
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | uuid | App-generated UUID |
| plate_number | text | Vehicle registration |
| condition | text | `Good` / `Fair` / `Poor` / `Critical` |
| kilometers | int4 | Odometer at check-in |
| check_in_date | timestamp | Auto or null |
| checked_by | uuid | FK → Users.id |
| repairs | text | Comma-joined selected repairs |
| additional_notes | text | Free-text observations |
| owner_name | text | Optional |
| status | text | Optional |

### `tasks`
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | uuid | App-generated UUID |
| truck_id | uuid | FK → trucks.id |
| mechanic_id | uuid | FK → Users.id |
| task_description | text | Repair item name |
| status | text | `pending` (default) or `completed` |
| notes | text | Mechanic's notes after completion |
| created_at | timestamp | Auto-set |
| completed_at | timestamp | Reserved for future use |

---

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Android Studio Hedgehog or newer
- Android device or emulator running API 26+
- Internet connection (Supabase is cloud-hosted)

### Setup

1. **Clone or unzip** the project and open it in Android Studio.

2. The Supabase connection is already configured in `SupabaseClient.kt` — no additional setup needed for the existing database.

3. **Build and run** on your device or emulator.

```bash
# Or build from the command line
./gradlew assembleDebug
```

### Adding Users to the Database

Users must be inserted directly into Supabase (there is no registration screen by design). Go to your Supabase project → Table Editor → `Users` and insert rows with:

```
name:  John Doe
email: john@vgarage.com
role:  mechanic        ← or "admin"
pin:   1234
```

---

## App Navigation

```
LoginActivity
    │
    ├── role == "admin"   ──► ReportsActivity
    │
    └── role == "mechanic" ──► DashboardActivity
                                    │
                                    ├── + NEW CHECK-IN ──► CheckInActivity
                                    │                           │
                                    │                           └── on submit ──► TasksActivity
                                    │
                                    └── VIEW TRUCKS IN SERVICE ──► TrucksInServiceActivity
                                                                        │
                                                                        └── tap truck ──► TasksActivity
```

---

## User Roles

### Mechanic
- Logs in → **Dashboard** showing fleet stats
- Taps **+ NEW CHECK-IN** to intake a vehicle:
  - Enter plate, kilometres, condition
  - Tick which repairs are needed (each becomes a task)
  - Add any extra notes
- Taps **VIEW TRUCKS IN SERVICE** to see all active trucks
- Opens any truck to view and tick off its task list
- Adds notes when marking a task as done

### Admin (Valentine)
- Logs in → **Reports** screen directly
- Sees four summary stats: Total, In Repair, Done, Urgent
- Scrolls to see each truck's repair progress
- Scrolls further to see each mechanic's completed tasks with their notes

---

## Architecture

The app follows a **Repository Pattern** with a single data layer:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│         UI Layer                │
│  (Activities + @Composables)    │
│  State: mutableStateOf          │
│  Async: LaunchedEffect /        │
│         rememberCoroutineScope  │
└────────────┬────────────────────┘
             │ suspend fun calls
┌────────────▼────────────────────┐
│      Repository Layer           │
│      GarageRepository (object)  │
│  - Single source of DB truth    │
│  - All try/catch handling       │
│  - Returns data classes         │
└────────────┬────────────────────┘
             │ Supabase Kotlin client
┌────────────▼────────────────────┐
│        Data Layer               │
│   Supabase / PostgreSQL         │
│   (cloud-hosted, HTTPS)         │
└─────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Refresh Pattern

Both `DashboardActivity` and `ReportsActivity` use an `onResume`-driven refresh:

```kotlin
private val refreshTrigger = mutableIntStateOf(0)

override fun onResume() {
    super.onResume()
    refreshTrigger.intValue++   // triggers LaunchedEffect to re-fetch
}
```

This ensures data is always current when navigating back to a screen.

---

## Key Classes

### `GarageRepository`
The only class that talks to the database. All Activities call this.

| Function | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `login(email, pin)` | Authenticate a user by email + PIN |
| `checkInTruck(...)` | Insert truck row + one task row per selected repair |
| `getActiveTruckByPlate(plate)` | Find an already-active truck to prevent duplicates |
| `getTasksForTruck(truckId)` | Load all tasks for a specific truck |
| `completeTask(taskId, notes)` | Mark a task done and save mechanic's notes |
| `getAllTrucks()` | Fetch all trucks (used for stats) |
| `getAllTasks()` | Fetch all tasks (used for stats) |
| `getAllUsers()` | Fetch all users (used for mechanic reports) |
| `getFleetStats()` | Compute FleetStats from trucks + tasks |

### `CurrentUser`
A Kotlin `object` (singleton) acting as the session store. Holds `id`, `name`, `role` after login. Cleared on logout. Tracks last activity for a 5-minute auto-logout.

### Data Classes
- `User` — maps to the `Users` table
- `Truck` — maps to the `trucks` table (nullable fields match DB nulls)
- `Task` — maps to the `tasks` table
- `FleetStats` — in-memory computed stats (not stored in DB)

